Description: Export the speech-to-text settings dialog, as ktextaddons 2.3.0 does
 Upstream exported SpeechToTextConfigureDialog in 2.3.0 and installs its header, so a
 program can open the library's own settings, where the person chooses the engine.
 2.1.2 kept it for its tests only, and Debian builds with BUILD_TESTING off, so no
 program could show the choice. Taken from the commit, the dialog's part only: its
 export, its documentation and its CamelCase header (the configure widget keeps its
 2.1.2 form, the version number is not taken).
Origin: backport, https://invent.kde.org/libraries/ktextaddons/-/commit/46f09141c23910dfe20278281c62bb88610ad2e2
Author: Laurent Montel
Applied-Upstream: v2.3.0, commit 46f09141 (Export class), 2026-10-05
Last-Update: 2026-11-22
